The correct answer is __**Start->All Programs->Microsoft Word**__.

 [IMAGE: https://cdn.repeatermock.com/tb/36f36cd5ece4186095afcf2ffbfb7b80cc04b6c2e3226e7477a419a9fbc96f85.png] **__Key Points__**

__

• To open a word processing package such as Microsoft Word, you typically start from the Start menu in Windows.

• The path is usually: **Start->All Programs->Microsoft Word**.

• Microsoft Word is a widely used word processing software developed by Microsoft.

• This method ensures that you are launching the correct application directly from its installed location.

 [IMAGE: https://cdn.repeatermock.com/tb/f13e2ad6582c16aa62a83672e2547ad20a01fddb61962a1acce42eb9a1a99caa.png] **Additional Information__**


• Microsoft Word is part of the Microsoft Office suite, which includes other productivity tools like Excel and PowerPoint.

• Modern versions of Microsoft Word can also be opened via desktop shortcuts or taskbar icons if they have been pinned there for easier access.

• Microsoft Word offers a wide range of features for document creation, editing, and formatting.

• Additionally, Microsoft Word can be accessed through Office Online, which allows users to work on documents from a web browser.
